---
interface Props {
  newCase: string | null;
  fix: string | null;
  repoUrl: string | null;
  contactEmail: string;
}
const { newCase, fix, repoUrl, contactEmail } = Astro.props;
---

<p class="lead">
  The database is open and lives on GitHub. Every value has a source and a status, and that is what
  makes it useful.
</p>

<div class="actions">
  {newCase && (
    <a class="btn" href={newCase} rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Report a case
    </a>
  )}
  {fix && (
    <a class="btn secondary" href={fix} rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Correct a value
    </a>
  )}
  {repoUrl && (
    <a class="btn secondary" href={repoUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">
      GitHub repository
    </a>
  )}
</div>
{!repoUrl && (
  <p class="notice">
    The GitHub repository is not public yet. In the meantime, write to{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
)}

<h2>What we accept</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    A <strong>case</strong>: a model whose advertised specs differ from the observed hardware.
  </li>
  <li>
    A missing <strong>SoC</strong>, or the correction of one of its hardware limits.
  </li>
  <li>
    A stronger <strong>source</strong> (datasheet, manufacturer page) for a value.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Review rules</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    A case becomes <strong>"confirmed"</strong> only with strong evidence: photos of the chips, a
    UART log or a storage test, plus a source.
  </li>
  <li>
    A value becomes <strong>"verified"</strong> with a datasheet or a manufacturer page, or with at
    least two independent sources (different domains) saying the same thing. A single forum source
    caps at "suspect".
  </li>
  <li>No copy-pasting from forums: summarise in your own words and add the link.</li>
  <li>
    Neutral wording: "reported case", "observed gap". No accusation against a seller or a brand.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Preparing your report</h2>
<h3>Photos of the chips</h3>
<p>
  Photograph each RAM and storage chip head-on, without glare, with the marking legible, plus an
  overall view of the board. State the exact model name and where it was bought (without naming an
  individual seller).
</p>
<h3>Commands under Linux</h3>
<pre><code>free -m
lsblk
cat /proc/cpuinfo | head -20
dmesg | grep -i -E "memory|mmc|dram"</code></pre>
<h3>Citing a source</h3>
<p>
  Give the exact address of the page, its title and the date you accessed it. For a datasheet, state
  the revision of the document.
</p>
